		<pubDate>Tue, 22 Jan 2013 00:17:43 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=996#comment-14062</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[Coming home the angels rejoice. You and Rabia showed me how, at the Abode, if in early spring, before the trees leafed, if just at sunrise you put your face on the floor and looked up at the &quot;Enter unhesitating...&quot; window new colors are seen. 
Happy Trails Khalid]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Coming home the angels rejoice. You and Rabia showed me how, at the Abode, if in early spring, before the trees leafed, if just at sunrise you put your face on the floor and looked up at the &#8220;Enter unhesitating&#8230;&#8221; window new colors are seen.<br />
Happy Trails Khalid</p>
]]></content:encoded>
	</item>
	<item>
		<title>By: khushi</title>
		<link>http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=996&#038;cpage=1#comment-14041</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[khushi]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sat, 19 Jan 2013 20:41:04 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=996#comment-14041</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[I have such fond memories of Aftab-her voice, her radiant smile, her dynamism. I recall one time when we were having an Abode reunion and had a Saturday night dance up on the Mountain with Stephen Pague. Aftab has always been about 20 years my senior, and there she was, cutting the rug! I couldn&#039;t believe how much energy came out of her on the dance floor! And I said to myself, I want to be like Aftab when I&#039;m that age ( whatever age it was- 70-75?) Such an inspiration!
Blessings dear Aftab on your journey home!
KHushi]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>I have such fond memories of Aftab-her voice, her radiant smile, her dynamism. I recall one time when we were having an Abode reunion and had a Saturday night dance up on the Mountain with Stephen Pague. Aftab has always been about 20 years my senior, and there she was, cutting the rug! I couldn&#8217;t believe how much energy came out of her on the dance floor! And I said to myself, I want to be like Aftab when I&#8217;m that age ( whatever age it was- 70-75?) Such an inspiration!<br />
Blessings dear Aftab on your journey home!<br />
KHushi</p>
]]></content:encoded>
	</item>
	<item>
		<title>By: Jehanara Wendy Tremayne</title>
		<link>http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=996&#038;cpage=1#comment-14040</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jehanara Wendy Tremayne]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sat, 19 Jan 2013 20:18:16 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=996#comment-14040</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[Aftab reflected something that settled my soul: what it is to be worked by time, to age as though in reverse, each day becoming  more luminous. As the days of my life turn, my hair begins to turn clear white, and my smiles are as river gorges around my eyes and mouth, her life appears as life raft to my own.  It says, &quot;die before you die,&quot; and I step forward trusting something unseen that is beauty beyond form. - XO Jehanara Tremayne]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Aftab reflected something that settled my soul: what it is to be worked by time, to age as though in reverse, each day becoming  more luminous. As the days of my life turn, my hair begins to turn clear white, and my smiles are as river gorges around my eyes and mouth, her life appears as life raft to my own.  It says, &#8220;die before you die,&#8221; and I step forward trusting something unseen that is beauty beyond form. &#8211; XO Jehanara Tremayne</p>
]]></content:encoded>
	</item>
	<item>
		<title>By: Azima Jackson</title>
		<link>http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=996&#038;cpage=1#comment-14013</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Azima Jackson]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Fri, 18 Jan 2013 01:48:14 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=996#comment-14013</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[Aftab, to me, was the keeper of prayer.  Everytime I would go to the Abode I could count on Aftab to be in the Meditation Hall praying at 7:00 am every morning.  She held that place for the Abode.  She was welcoming when I arrived at any time.  She had nothing but encouragement and support for me as a cheraga, as a Sufi, as a person.  She shared herself fully and her journey.  She was vulnerable, and joyful, authentic and real.  I loved her.

Azima]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Aftab, to me, was the keeper of prayer.  Everytime I would go to the Abode I could count on Aftab to be in the Meditation Hall praying at 7:00 am every morning.  She held that place for the Abode.  She was welcoming when I arrived at any time.  She had nothing but encouragement and support for me as a cheraga, as a Sufi, as a person.  She shared herself fully and her journey.  She was vulnerable, and joyful, authentic and real.  I loved her.</p>
<p>Azima</p>
]]></content:encoded>
	</item>
	<item>
		<title>By: nurunnahar</title>
		<link>http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=996&#038;cpage=1#comment-14004</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[nurunnahar]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 17 Jan 2013 07:55:14 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=996#comment-14004</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[i met aftab at the abode during my suluk training. and i remember the beautiful morning meditations with her. she sat on her little chair in front of us and guided us so vividly through the purification practices and the prayers. afterwards she used to do her physical exercises (the 5 buddhistic treasures or so ...). and one day i asked her if i could join her. and i realized she had a very good physical condition, despite her age. she told me that she did these practices every day to keep her shape. 
she was such a sunshine, really expressing the deeper meaning of her name which means &#039;sun&#039;. thank you, aftab, for the beautiful shared moments!
love,
nurunnahar]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>i met aftab at the abode during my suluk training. and i remember the beautiful morning meditations with her. she sat on her little chair in front of us and guided us so vividly through the purification practices and the prayers. afterwards she used to do her physical exercises (the 5 buddhistic treasures or so &#8230;). and one day i asked her if i could join her. and i realized she had a very good physical condition, despite her age. she told me that she did these practices every day to keep her shape.<br />
she was such a sunshine, really expressing the deeper meaning of her name which means &#8216;sun&#8217;. thank you, aftab, for the beautiful shared moments!<br />
love,<br />
nurunnahar</p>
]]></content:encoded>
	</item>
